  "description": "Vulgar Display of Power is the sixth studio album by American groove metal band Pantera. Released on February 24, 1992, through Atco Records, it was the band's second collaboration with producer Terry Date, after having worked with him on their breakthrough album Cowboys from Hell (1990). The band sought to make an album heavier than Cowboys from Hell, particularly motivated by the more commercial sound Metallica had adopted on their self-titled album, which was released during the album's recording.",
